  "verify": "Pins from Waveshare's demo code and schematic (https://github.com/waveshareteam/ESP32-C6-Touch-AMOLED-1.8). This is the V2 revision (CO5300 panel, CST820 touch, 16-column offset); a V1 board (SH8601, FT3168, no offset) has the same pins and needs the other record - the vendor tells them apart by which touch address answers, 0x15 or 0x38. Every pin recorded here is the same in the vendor's code and on the schematic. The glass has rounded corners of radius 55 px: Waveshare gives none, and this is the measurement from the owner's ESP32-S3-Touch-AMOLED-1.8 V2 (2026-10-22), the same 1.8 inch 368 x 448 AMOLED (SH8601 on V1, CO5300 with the same 16-column gap on V2); not measured on a C6 board. On the board and not in this preset: TF card: this chip has one SPI controller and the panel has it (Waveshare's own code runs one or the other). Brightness is a command to the panel, not a backlight pin. Compiled; not run on a board here.",
